    <string name="calm_onb_notifications_title">Notifications</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_notifications_why">Shows a silent countdown while a session runs, one warning before it ends, and “End now”.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_notifications_reduced">Without it: sessions still end on time, but you cannot see the time left.</string>

    <string name="calm_onb_overlay_title">Display over other apps</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_overlay_why">Lets the calm time\'s-up card appear over the app when a session ends, with Go home, Extend and the override.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_overlay_reduced">Without it: a “Time\'s up” notification appears instead, and nothing is covered.</string>

    <string name="calm_onb_usage_title">Usage access</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_usage_why">Lets the launcher check that the tracked app is really in front before showing the card, and count opens that did not go through the launcher. Only package names and times are read.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_usage_reduced">Without it: no card is shown; a “Time\'s up” notification appears instead.</string>

    <string name="calm_onb_alarms_title">Alarms and reminders</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_alarms_why">A backup alarm ends the session on time even if Android stops the timer. Optional.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_alarms_reduced">Without it: if the timer is stopped, the session closes the next time you return to the launcher.</string>

    <string name="calm_onb_battery_title">Battery: Unrestricted</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_battery_why">Keeps the session timer alive. On Samsung also set Settings → Apps → Calm Launcher → Battery → Unrestricted, and keep the app off the Sleeping apps lists.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_battery_reduced">Without it: the phone may stop the timer; sessions are then closed late, and the home screen says so.</string>

    <string name="calm_onb_exempt_title">Apps that are never limited</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_exempt_why">Phone, messages, maps, camera, clock and Settings are already exempt. These apps were found on your phone; keep ticked the ones that must always open straight away.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_exempt_reduced">You can change this any time in Screen time limits.</string>
    <string name="calm_onb_exempt_none">None of the common messaging, banking, authenticator or transport apps were found. You can make any app exempt in Screen time limits.</string>
